.TH PROVIUM-COVERAGE 1 "" "Provium 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
provium-coverage \- Summarize Test Events by Metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B provium-coverage
.RI [ \-from\ PATH ]\ [ \-by\ KEY ]\ [ \-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the length-prefixed MessagePack stream produced by Provium and group
test outcomes by a metadata key. The default key is spec.
This is test-metadata coverage, not compiler line or branch coverage.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-from " PATH"
Read PATH instead of standard input.
.TP
.BR \-by " KEY"
Group outcomes by KEY instead of spec.
.TP
.B \-json
Write JSON instead of the text summary.
.TP
.BR \-help , " \-version"
Print help or the program version. Short forms are \-h and \-V.
.SH EXAMPLES
Save a run's events, then summarize them:
.PP
.nf
provium tests/ \-save-events events.msgpack
provium-coverage \-from events.msgpack \-by spec
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR provium (1)
